    "long_instructions": "**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Encode your features and create a feature matrix—your `inputs`.\r\n- Define a list of labels—your `outputs`.\r\n- In your Project Planning Guide, respond to the question in **Step 5: Modeling**, under **Encoding Inputs and Outputs**.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember to cast your numeric data using `float` or `int`.\r\n\r\nAlso remember you can use `OneHotEncoder` to encode data with multiple categories.\r\n\r\n```\r\nencoder = OneHotEncoder()\r\nencoding = encoder.fit_transform(\r\n    [[row[\"FEATURE\"]] for row in data]\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlso notice that `create_matrix` is imported for you from `helpers.py`. You can use it to assemble a feature matrix from individual encodings.\r\n\r\n```\r\nfeatures = [feature0, feature1, feature2]\r\ninputs = create_matrix(features)\r\n```",
